{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00276",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 3.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Afternoon, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.5,
      "end_seconds": 9.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "No trouble at all, come in. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.33,
      "end_seconds": 23.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.25,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed. It's my heart racing, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.65,
      "end_seconds": 27.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.35,
      "end_seconds": 31.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Just since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.41,
      "end_seconds": 36.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Okay, keep going. What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.52,
      "end_seconds": 43.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "I, I'd say a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.17,
      "end_seconds": 48.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.68,
      "end_seconds": 76.52,
      "duration_seconds": 26.84,
      "text": "Right, you know, when it starts I tend to get shaky hands as well. The shaky hands? That's been since yesterday. And I've been feeling anxious and jittery as well, for about two weeks. And, And I've been feeling hot and sweaty as well, you know, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.61,
      "end_seconds": 80.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Let me measure a few things."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.2,
      "end_seconds": 91.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Rest your hand here..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.54,
      "end_seconds": 114.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 106, blood pressure 132 over 71, saturation 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.26,
      "end_seconds": 120.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.62,
      "end_seconds": 124.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Almost done with this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.97,
      "end_seconds": 144.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "There's a fine tremor in the outstretched hands, and your palms are warm and moist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.06,
      "end_seconds": 149.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Stay still while I have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.74,
      "end_seconds": 171.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Your thyroid feels a little enlarged and smooth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.85,
      "end_seconds": 176.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.97,
      "end_seconds": 184.96,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Any diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.51,
      "end_seconds": 189.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, um, no diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 191.46,
      "end_seconds": 198.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Um, uh, actually, doctor, I did notice diarrhoea. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.5,
      "end_seconds": 206.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "No, you know, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.1,
      "end_seconds": 217.99,
      "duration_seconds": 9.89,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any lump in the neck, chest pain or shortness of breath at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.84,
      "end_seconds": 228.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.14,
      "text": "So, I haven't had lump in the neck, chest pain or shortness of breath, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.7,
      "end_seconds": 232.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.78,
      "end_seconds": 234.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.39,
      "end_seconds": 238.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.18,
      "end_seconds": 242.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I mean, no, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.37,
      "end_seconds": 247.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Before I prescribe anything, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.52,
      "end_seconds": 252.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Not that I know, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 253.69,
      "end_seconds": 261.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to ibuprofen once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.07,
      "end_seconds": 270.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Maybe, um, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.83,
      "end_seconds": 277.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. Tell me what you take day to day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 277.77,
      "end_seconds": 298.11,
      "duration_seconds": 20.34,
      "text": "It's sodium valproate, 500 milligrams, twice a day for the fits, doctor. Oh, she takes diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed. So, she is on sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.73,
      "end_seconds": 302.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Levetiracetam I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.57,
      "end_seconds": 313.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Is there anything medical in your background?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.44,
      "end_seconds": 339.74,
      "duration_seconds": 25.3,
      "text": "I, I have epilepsy, for five years. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. Yes, arthritis in my knees. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Migraines, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.38,
      "end_seconds": 341.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "And then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.82,
      "end_seconds": 356.73,
      "duration_seconds": 13.91,
      "text": "Right, yes, epilepsy and arthritis in your knees are known to us, good to have that clear. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.53,
      "end_seconds": 377.01,
      "duration_seconds": 18.48,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago. I skip breakfast most days. I walk for about half an hour most days. I work in an office, mostly sitting at a desk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.63,
      "end_seconds": 392.25,
      "duration_seconds": 13.62,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: It points towards an overactive thyroid. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I can't rule out anxiety yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.59,
      "end_seconds": 415.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "I'm going to order a thyroid test, for hyperthyroid symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.03,
      "end_seconds": 418.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.68,
      "end_seconds": 446.86,
      "duration_seconds": 26.18,
      "text": "I'm sending you for a thyroid scan because of hyperthyroidism. We'll begin with propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. You take it by mouth. It's for palpitations and tremor. Limit tea, coffee and anything that speeds up the heart for now. I think an endocrinologist should see you too. Book a review after the results are back. Thanks for coming in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 448.59,
      "end_seconds": 450.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Thanks so much, doctor."
    }
  ]
}